  "title": "Magnetic recovery does not measure all the iron in a mixture",
  "original_forecast": "Reconcile what the magnetic operation actually moves with the metallic and oxide identities. The recovered fraction must not be reported as total elemental iron without accounting for iron remaining in hematite.",
  "original_limitations": [
    "Real hematite magnetism and grain-size effects are more subtle than a binary model. Use the operation's actual species selectivity; no magnetic-susceptibility calibration is assumed."
